The keys 4, 2, *, 7, 9 are pressed in turn. '*' deletes the last digit. What is printed on the screen at the end?

```
char girilen[5] = "";
int hane = 0;
char tuslar[] = {'4', '2', '*', '7', '9'};
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
  char t = tuslar[i];
  if (t == '*') {
    if (hane > 0) { hane--; girilen[hane] = '\0'; }
  } else {
    girilen[hane] = t;
    hane++;
    girilen[hane] = '\0';
  }
}
Serial.println(girilen);
```

